{
  "$comment": "AN-FORCE-UPDATE (R1110, R1113). The ONE home for what GET /api/v1/android/minimum-version answers for each value of its one server setting, ANDROID_MINIMUM_VERSION_CODE. Read by BOTH sides of R204's join: web/tests/unit/api/android-minimum-version.test.ts drives the REAL route handler with each `setting` and requires its response to equal `body` exactly; android/app/src/test/kotlin/ch/monreleve/app/update/MinimumVersionFixtureTest.kt hands each `body` to the app's REAL client parsing and requires `minimum`. So a renamed field, a changed `service` or a different reading of a setting fails both builds. `setting` null means the variable is UNSET. Unset, empty, blank or malformed all answer `minimumVersionCode: null` - NO minimum, said explicitly, never a guessed number - so the mechanism ships inert.",
